        "title": "fix: keep repair reviews on the pinned base and renew post-flight credentials",
        "body": "## Reproduced defect\n\nLarge contributor-branch repair runs cannot publish even after the coherent timeout-budget fix.\n\nRun `29134881957` and run `29136885669` reproduce two independent control-plane defects:\n\n1. Inner review-fix attempts compare against newly fetched live branch tips instead of the immutable target-base snapshot captured for the repair. Each attempt therefore requests another rebase, consuming all bounded attempts.\n2. After a long execution, post-flight outcome-comment lookup uses an expired credential and throws `Bad credentials (HTTP 401)`, masking the actual repair result.\n\nObserved moving bases:\n- first run: `67e1d439` → `b7156ce` → `7febbad0` → `00740056`\n- second run: `4a00b96b` → `ffc8051c` → `8a29e8c9` → `cd7a2178`\n\nIn the first run, the first three rebased trees passed changed-surface validation, diff checks, and conflict scans. The final failure was in a base-identical file outside the repair diff. Both runs then ended during status publication with HTTP 401.\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- Capture one immutable target-base SHA at contributor-repair start.\n- Pass that SHA explicitly to every inner edit, validation, review, and review-fix worker.\n- Inner review must not fetch or compare with a later live branch tip.\n- After a pass against the pinned base, allow exactly one deterministic final live-base synchronization. If it changes the tree, run exactly one validation/review on the synchronized tree before publication.\n- Classify failures in byte-identical base files outside the repair diff as external base blockers.\n- Obtain a fresh short-lived target credential immediately before post-flight GitHub reads/writes.\n- Preserve the repaired commit/tree and machine-readable result when publication fails; publication errors must not replace the actual repair outcome.\n\n## Acceptance coverage\n\n- A moving-base fixture advances the branch before every simulated review; every inner review still receives the original pinned SHA and no inner rebase is requested.\n- Final synchronization occurs no more than once and gets one exact synchronized-tree validation/review.\n- Generated-file reconciliation is retained during final synchronization.\n- An expired initial credential is refreshed before comment lookup/publication.\n- A forced publication 401 leaves a recoverable repair result/artifact.\n\nPreserve exact-head CI/review/security gates, bounded attempts, mergeability checks, credential scope, cleanup, and failure reporting.",
