        "kind": "issue",
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "fix: pin repair review base and refresh credentials before post-flight publication",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nLarge automerge repairs still cannot complete after #485 and #488.\n\nTwo deterministic failures are reproduced by OpenClaw PR #103331:\n\n1. **Review-fix workers chase live `origin/main` instead of the pinned repair base.** Each exact-tree review fetches whatever `main` became during the run and emits a rebase finding. The repair loop then rebases, validates, and repeats until all four attempts are exhausted.\n2. **Long runs use an expired GitHub credential during post-flight publication.** After the review loop, `appendAutomergeRepairOutcomeComment` calls `gh` with a stale token and throws `Bad credentials (HTTP 401)`, preventing durable status/publication and discarding an otherwise useful repaired tree.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n- Run 29134881957: review bases advanced `67e1d439` → `b7156ce` → `7febbad0` → `00740056`; the first three rebases passed `pnpm check:changed`, `git diff --check`, and conflict scans. Final validation failed only in a base-identical Telegram lint file. Post-flight then failed 401.\n- Run 29136885669: even with explicit pinned-base instructions, reviews advanced `4a00b96b` → `ffc8051c` → `8a29e8c9` → `cd7a2178`, each requesting another rebase. Post-flight again failed 401.\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- Capture one immutable target-base SHA when contributor repair begins.\n- All edit, validation, and review-fix attempts must compare against that pinned SHA, not a freshly fetched moving branch tip.\n- Do not report base drift during the bounded inner loop as a repair finding.\n- After the repaired tree passes against the pinned base, perform exactly one deterministic final synchronization with current `main`; if that changes the tree, validate/review that synchronized tree once before publication.\n- Preserve generated-file reconciliation such as `docs/docs_map.md` during the single final sync.\n- Refresh/reissue the target write credential immediately before post-flight GitHub reads/writes, or route publication through a short-lived fresh token.\n- A post-flight status failure must preserve the repaired commit/tree and machine-readable result rather than masking the actual repair outcome.\n\n## Acceptance coverage\n\n- A moving-main fixture advances the branch between four simulated review calls; every inner review still receives the original pinned base and does not request rebases.\n- Final synchronization occurs at most once and is followed by one exact synchronized-tree validation/review.\n- Base-identical failures outside the repair diff are classified as external base blockers.\n- An expired initial token is replaced before outcome-comment lookup/publication.\n- A publication 401 produces a recoverable preserved result and does not lose the validated repair artifact.\n\n## Safety\n\nKeep exact-head CI/review/security gates, bounded attempts, mergeability checks, credential scope, cleanup, and failure reporting unchanged.",
